# Tab containers from dubna (dubna/src/chrome/browser/containers, dubna/patches/containers.patch);
# the Android side is src/chrome/browser/containers/platform and android/ (docs/containers.md).
# A tab stays in the container its WebContents starts in, so these hooks only create tabs there:
# - TabImpl.java: a tab Java creates without a WebContents gets one from Containers, which picks
#   its opener's container for a link, or Settings' container for a new tab. So does a tab whose
#   saved state can't be restored.
# - browser_navigator_android.cc: a tab Navigate() opens from a container tab stays in it.
# - TabModelJniBridge.java: a blocked popup allowed later keeps its container tab as parent.
# - ChromeTabCreator.java: such a tab doesn't take the spare tab custom tabs warm up, which is
#   outside containers.
# - web_contents_state.cc: a tab restores in its container after a restart.
# - android_live_tab_context.cc, session_restore_android.cc: a closed tab reopens in it.
# - chrome/android/BUILD.gn, chrome_java_ext_sources.gni: our Java and its JNI.
# - generated_resources.grd: dubna's strings. The Android ones are ours, with Polish.
